WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.525
The Great Wall of China is one of the most recognizable landmarks in the world. It

2
00:00:06.526 --> 00:00:14.957
is the world's longest structure. In fact, some astronauts have said they could see it from space! Curving

3
00:00:14.958 --> 00:00:25.636
across the land like a sleeping dragon, it follows almost the entire northern border of China for more than twenty thousand kilometers. You might

4
00:00:25.637 --> 00:00:30.497
ask why a nation would need a wall along its border. The Chinese

5
00:00:30.498 --> 00:00:37.794
people built the Great Wall to protect their civilization from attacking tribes in the north. But the Great

6
00:00:37.795 --> 00:00:47.815
Wall of China took over two thousand years to complete, and during this time an incredible amount of history unfolded. Qin Dynasty (221 BC

7
00:00:47.816 --> 00:00:59.068
to 206 BC) The Qin dynasty was a short-lived but important dynasty because its first ruler, Emperor Qin Shi Huang, was a very

8
00:00:59.069 --> 00:01:04.631
influential emperor. He unified China and started the construction of the Great Wall

9
00:01:04.632 --> 00:01:08.814
of China. He used all his authority to get the

10
00:01:08.815 --> 00:01:13.284
wall built. The builders used the hang-tu method of

11
00:01:13.285 --> 00:01:22.485
construction. They erected two temporary barriers parallel to each other and packed a layer of dirt, stones, and wood between

12
00:01:22.486 --> 00:01:31.290
them. After many layers were built up, the temporary barriers were removed, leaving a tall, thick earthen wall.

13
00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:38.220
Watchtowers were constructed along the wall so that soldiers could see enemy armies approaching.

14
00:01:38.221 --> 00:01:47.012
If invaders attacked, the soldiers lit a fire, and the smoke was a signal to warn the soldiers in the other watchtowers. Back

15
00:01:47.013 --> 00:01:54.351
then there were no mechanical tools to help with construction, so all the work was done by hand. It was

16
00:01:54.352 --> 00:02:03.687
back-breaking labor, and life was very hard for the workers, especially because Emperor Qin was ruthless. It is

17
00:02:03.688 --> 00:02:08.591
believed that hundreds of thousands of men died building it. The Qin dynasty

18
00:02:08.592 --> 00:02:15.784
did not last very long after the death of Emperor Qin Shi Huang in 210 BC. According to some

19
00:02:15.785 --> 00:02:23.575
accounts, he was able to build over 2,500 kilometers of the Great Wall. Han Dynasty (206 BC

20
00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:32.099
to 220 AD) After the fall of the Qin dynasty, a leader named Liu Bang came to power and established the

21
00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:44.763
Han dynasty. By the time Emperor Wu Di, the seventh emperor of the Han dynasty, came to power in 141 BC, the Great Wall had deteriorated and needed major

22
00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:49.152
repairs. Wu Di wanted to rebuild and extend the

23
00:02:49.153 --> 00:02:53.763
wall. His workers also used the hang-tu method of

24
00:02:53.764 --> 00:03:00.818
construction, so the architecture of the wall changed very little from that of the section built during the Qin dynasty.

25
00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:07.557
Wu Di's workers, however, had better working conditions, and got paid for their service.

26
00:03:07.558 --> 00:03:13.660
During Wu Di's reign, another large section of the Great Wall was completed. It

27
00:03:13.661 --> 00:03:20.462
was also during the reign of Wu Di that China started trading its riches with countries in the west. Chinese traders

28
00:03:20.463 --> 00:03:30.914
traveled to Central Asia, the Middle East, and even as far as Rome, bringing silk, paper, and spices to Europe. This long

29
00:03:30.915 --> 00:03:39.684
trading route was called the Silk Road, and the main route of the Silk Road closely followed the curves of the Great Wall. Life in villages

30
00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:49.057
along the wall was prosperous and peaceful during this time, but this era eventually came to an end. After the death of

31
00:03:49.058 --> 00:04:00.247
Emperor Wu Di in 87 BC, the Han dynasty slowly deteriorated and finally ended in 220 AD. It wasn't until a thousand

32
00:04:00.248 --> 00:04:09.747
years later, during the Ming dynasty, that the Great Wall became an impressive structure once again. The Ming Dynasty (1368 AD

33
00:04:09.748 --> 00:04:15.025
to 1644 AD) What we see of the Great Wall today was built during the

34
00:04:15.026 --> 00:04:23.517
Ming dynasty. The first emperor and his successors maintained the Great Wall very carefully, and strengthened it to keep

35
00:04:23.518 --> 00:04:30.541
invaders out. The wall became an important project for each of the Ming

36
00:04:30.542 --> 00:04:39.771
emperors. By the time of this dynasty, new inventions had become available to help the workers with

37
00:04:39.772 --> 00:04:44.104
construction. Workers still used the hang-tu method of construction,

38
00:04:44.105 --> 00:04:52.159
but this time they packed the dirt and stones between two solid brick walls to make it more stable.

39
00:04:52.161 --> 00:04:59.636
They made the top of the wall wide enough for horse carriages to travel, and built more watchtowers. Now,

40
00:04:59.637 --> 00:05:07.334
instead of smoke signals, soldiers used gunpowder rockets to warn of an approaching enemy. Another improvement

41
00:05:07.335 --> 00:05:13.247
made to the wall during the Ming dynasty was a drainage system. Until then

42
00:05:13.248 --> 00:05:20.398
rainwater slowly collected in the wall, making it deteriorate more quickly. After the

43
00:05:20.399 --> 00:05:29.144
last Ming emperor died in 1620, construction on the wall ceased. The era had ended. From the Qing

44
00:05:29.145 --> 00:05:38.271
Dynasty to Today For the next four centuries, China was ruled by the Qing dynasty, which did not need the wall to protect

45
00:05:38.272 --> 00:05:47.215
its borders. By the time the Qing dynasty collapsed and the Communist Party took control, the Great Wall was

46
00:05:47.216 --> 00:05:55.080
nearly forgotten. But in 1980 the Chinese government decided to restore the Great Wall and show it to the

47
00:05:55.081 --> 00:06:10.233
world. Today it is one of the most visited tourist attractions on earth, a silent witness to the many battles, wars, and changing empires of China's history.

